What happens: The Segment is wrapped inside an IP header.

What gets added:

Source IP Address: 192.168.1.8 (Where this originated).

Destination IP Address: 142.250.190.46 (The global destination across the internet).

TTL (Time to Live): Hop counter to prevent infinite routing loops.

The Analogy: Placing the office envelope inside a FedEx postal box with your home address and Google's data center street address printed on the outside.

